{"chunk_id": "7a093a8647ef", "text": "Ravana, having approached Sita in the guise of an ascetic, reveals his true identity after she fiercely rebukes his advances and warns him that harming Rama\u2019s wife will bring certain destruction. Enraged, the titan king casts off his disguise and manifests his terrifying form with ten heads and twenty arms, boasting of his cosmic power. Ignoring her defiance, he violently seizes Sita and lifts her into his golden chariot, which rises into the sky. As Ravana carries her away through the air, Sita cries out desperately for Rama and Lakshmana, condemns Ravana\u2019s fate, and calls upon the forest, the Godavari river, and all living creatures to bear witness and deliver news of her abduction. Spotting the vulture Jatayu, she begs him to tell Rama what has happened, setting in motion the coming pursuit and battle.\nRavana reveals his true form, seizes Sita, and carries her away in his chariot as she cries for Rama and calls on nature to bear witness.\nThemes: abduction, dharma and violation, power and arrogance, loyalty to Rama, appeal to nature as witness", "vector": [0.01054542325437069, -0.020132776349782944, 0.006526851560920477, 0.005602048244327307, -0.017072275280952454, 0.014344437047839165, -0.03912119194865227, -0.005838239099830389, -0.02646668255329132, -0.027624351903796196, 0.017870666459202766, 0.027331607416272163, 0.010611956007778645, 0.01550210453569889, -0.0031835867557674646, 0.006649937015026808, 0.04191556200385094, -0.013945240527391434, 0.01856260560452938, -0.024364251643419266, 0.0021539940498769283, -0.017750907689332962, -0.005997917149215937, 0.013785562478005886, -0.024271106347441673, -0.01200914103537798, 0.02580135688185692, -0.037417955696582794, 0.02767757698893547, -0.015156134963035583, -0.014450889080762863, -0.011589985340833664, -0.008163554593920708, -0.01570170186460018, -0.02475014142692089, 0.010691794566810131, -0.006546811666339636, -0.025082804262638092, 0.007458308711647987, -0.0